# Review checklist (after generation; no test execution)

Apply this before reporting that code generation is complete. Fix code/documentation issues; do not tick a box that is not true. The AI must not execute Playwright tests. The user runs them manually.

## Case and traceability

- [ ] `docs/manual-test-cases/TC-NNN-*.md` exists, Status/Automated/Spec are correct
- [ ] README traceability row added
- [ ] Title, tags, and TC id match the spec

## Live site (not invented)

- [ ] Every new locator, message, path, and endpoint was verified on automationexercise.com
- [ ] `data-qa` used via `getByTestId` where present
- [ ] Ads handled (`dismissAds`) on click-heavy UI flows
- [ ] API asserts `httpStatus` **and** `responseCode`; form-urlencoded

## Spec quality

- [ ] `import { test, expect } from '../../src/fixtures'` (path adjusted)
- [ ] No selectors, URLs, `waitForTimeout`, `any`, or `console.log` in the spec
- [ ] `test.step` per manual step group; 2+ meaningful assertions
- [ ] Parallel-safe unique data; API user deleted in teardown that cannot throw

## Static validation (no test execution)

- [ ] No Playwright test command or npm test script was executed by the AI
- [ ] `npm run lint` and `npm run typecheck` were run only if confirmed to be static-only; otherwise marked `Not run`
- [ ] Static-check failures, if any, are reported accurately; assertions are not weakened to silence issues
- [ ] Agent mistakes appended to `docs/ai-review-log.md`

## Manual execution handoff (user-owned)

- [ ] Exact command for the user to execute the generated spec is provided
- [ ] State clearly that the AI did not execute the test and no pass/fail result is claimed
- [ ] Case remains `Status: Ready` until the user confirms a successful manual run
- [ ] Update status to `Automated` only after user confirmation
